    <validation>
      <review type="Independent external review">
        <common:dataQualityIndicators>
          <common:dataQualityIndicator name="Technological representativeness" value="Very good"/>
          <common:dataQualityIndicator name="Time representativeness" value="Very good"/>
          <common:dataQualityIndicator name="Geographical representativeness" value="Very good"/>
          <common:dataQualityIndicator name="Completeness" value="Very good"/>
        </common:dataQualityIndicators>
        <common:reviewDetails>The study is very representative from a geographical and technological point of view. From a temporal point of view, as the data refer to the two-year period 2020-2021, the representativeness is considered very good. For the tomato pulp packaging, the completeness is considered very good.&#13;
&#13;
Companies provided the number of pieces, weight, and packaging data sheets. For the companies that provided only the number of pieces, the weight of the packaging was calculated from the weight reported by the other companies.&#13;
Some of the packaging used by the companies (bins, lids, and pallets) are defined by the companies as durable materials; therefore, the companies were asked about their reuse. Compared to the quantities reported by the companies, it was found that about 50 percent of the total durable packaging used was already in its second use, with an expected reuse of at least three times.&#13;
&#13;
The inventory data relating to the various processes within the system's boundaries are therefore to be considered reasonably representative of the supply chain under study, as they can to all intents and purposes be considered average data for the same. The quality of the data used in the study is considered to be good and the data were for the most part measured; where they were calculated or came from literature, they were all checked by experts.&#13;
Allocation was avoided as far as possible by dividing the unitary process into two or more sub-processes and collecting environmental data on these sub-processes.&#13;
When allocation could not be avoided, as in the case of products obtained during processing, the inputs and outputs of the system were divided between its different products and by-products.&#13;
The allocation was generally based on mass (e.g. for waste treatment, waste water and energy used).&#13;
The review  was performed  in compliance with Arcadia Metodology: “Metodologia per gli studi di filiera della Banca Dati italiana LCA” and ISO 14040-44 norms. The dataset has been assessed limited to the foreground data collected during the supply chain studies.&#13;
Each dataset has been evaluated based on the following 4 criteria:&#13;
1. Technological Representativeness;  2. Time Representativeness; 3. Geographical Representativeness; 4. Reliability (A)&#13;
In this contest the Reliability is very good&#13;
</common:reviewDetails>
